# Splendid! Splendid!
Tamil title: அருமை! அருமை!

At Thirukkattupalli, after speaking in praise of Sir Sivaswami Iyer's service, the Honourable Srinivasa Sastri unveiled a portrait of Sir C. P. Ramaswami Iyer.

S. R. Balasubramaniam Iyer, headmaster of the Sivaswami Iyer School, delivered the vote of thanks.

Vaidyanatha Iyer.

Justice Varadachariar, Justice Patanjali Sastri, Sir Radhakrishna Iyer, T. T. Krishnamachari, Rao Bahadur G. A. Natesan Iyer, and Dr T. S. S. Rajan Iyengar sent messages of felicitation.

This appeared in *Swadesamitran*, edited by C. R. Srinivasa Iyengar.

Behold how a community protects its own!

(*Dravida Nadu*, 13-2-1944)

---NOTES---
No separate article heading is visible in the OCR source. The Tamil and English display titles are conservatively derived from the canonical filename; the verbatim source block remains unchanged.
“வைத்தியநாத ஐயர்” appears as an isolated fragment after the vote-of-thanks sentence. It is retained as a separate fragment in English because its syntactic role cannot be established safely from the OCR alone.
The closing sentence uses “இனம்” polemically in the source; “community” preserves the immediate argument without silently expanding it.
